-- title:
--   Base change of the j-chart from the cyclotomic constants
-- statement:
--   Fix a prime $q$, an $M'\neq 0$ with $q\nmid M'$, and a prime $\ell$ with $\ell\equiv 11 \pmod{12}$ and $\ell\mid M'$. Let $L$ be a field of characteristic zero containing a primitive $q$-th root of unity $\zeta$ and a primitive $q\ell$-th root of unity $\xi$ with $\zeta=\xi^{\ell}$, such that some ring homomorphism $L\to\mathbb{C}$ carries $\xi$ to $\exp(2\pi i/(q\ell))$. Let $H_1\le(\mathbb{Z}/q^2M')^{\times}$ be the subgroup of units congruent to $1$ modulo $q$ and to $1$ modulo $\ell$, i.e. the intersection of the kernel of reduction to $(\mathbb{Z}/q)^{\times}$ with the kernel of reduction to $(\mathbb{Z}/\ell)^{\times}$, and let $K$ be the intermediate field of $L\subset L((\mathfrak q))$ obtained by adjoining to $L$ the coefficientwise image of the $q$-expansion function field [`ModularCurve.xHFunctionField (q ^ 2 * M') H₁`](def/ModularCurve_XH.html#L79) of level $H_1$ in $q^2M'$. Let $A$ be a discrete valuation ring with fraction field $L$ and algebraically closed residue field, with $q$ in its maximal ideal, $\zeta$ in the image of $A$, uniformiser $\varpi$, and with an $A$-algebra structure on $K$ compatible with $A\to L\to K$; let $j\in K$, $j\neq0$, have Laurent expansion the image of the $j$-series [`ModularCurve.jq`](def/ModularCurve_X0.html#L157) under the coefficient map $\mathbb{Q}\to L$. Write $C=$ `chartAlgFin A K j` for the integral closure of $A[j]$ in $K$, that is the elements of $K$ integral over the $A$-subalgebra generated by $j$. Let $y$ be a point of $\operatorname{Spec} C$ whose prime ideal is maximal and contains the image of $\varpi$, and assume $y$ is supersingular in the sense that for every algebraically closed field $\Omega$ of characteristic $q$ and every ring homomorphism $\varphi:C\to\Omega$ with kernel $y$, the element $\varphi(j)$ lies in [`ModularCurve.ssJSet q Ω`](def/ModularCurve_SupersingularModuli.html#L7), i.e. every elliptic curve over $\Omega$ with that $j$-invariant has no nonzero point killed by $q$. Descent data are fixed as follows: $L_0$ is a cyclotomic extension of $\mathbb{Q}$ of order $q\ell$ containing a primitive $q$-th root $\zeta_0$ and a primitive $q\ell$-th root $\xi_0$, $i:L_0\to L$ is a ring homomorphism with $i\zeta_0=\zeta$, $i\xi_0=\xi$; $A_0$ is a discrete valuation ring with fraction field $L_0$ and uniformiser $\varpi_0$, equipped with an injective local homomorphism $A_0\to A$ compatible with $i$ and such that an element $x\in L_0$ lies in the image of $A_0$ exactly when $i(x)$ lies in the image of $A$; and $K_0$, $j_0\neq 0$ are the corresponding intermediate field of $L_0\subset L_0((\mathfrak q))$ and the corresponding $j$-element over $L_0$, with $C_0=$ `chartAlgFin A₀ K₀ j₀`. The conclusion asserts the existence of a ring homomorphism $c_K:K_0\to K$ acting coefficientwise by $i$ on Laurent expansions and sending $j_0$ to $j$, of a ring homomorphism $c:C_0\to C$ inducing $c_K$ on underlying elements and compatible with $A_0\to A$, and of a ring isomorphism $\beta:A\otimes_{A_0}C_0\xrightarrow{\sim}C$ with $\beta(a\otimes b)=a\cdot c(b)$; moreover the contracted ideal $c^{-1}(y)$ is maximal in $C_0$, contains the image of $\varpi_0$, and is again supersingular in the above sense for $j_0$.
--
--   This is the statement that formation of the $j$-finite chart of the two-chart integral model commutes with the flat base change $A_0\to A$, so that the chart algebra over $A$ is obtained from the one over the cyclotomic ring $A_0$ by tensoring, and that the chosen supersingular maximal point descends to $A_0$; it is the $\Gamma_1(\ell)$-type auxiliary-level variant, valid for all primes $q$ including $q=2,3$. It is used to transport computations of completed local rings at supersingular points of the full-level model down to the field generated by the cyclotomic constants $\mathbb{Q}(\xi)$.
-- source:
--   https://github.com/anthropics/fermats-last-theorem/blob/aa2d8b34692b16c70f699536de0d8e75b9a3e9ef/Theorems/Thm_ModularCurve_FullLevel_AuxLevelOne_exists_chartAlgFin_tensorProduct_ringEquiv_of_cyclotomicConstants_of_isAlgClosed_of_isPrimitiveRoot_mul_of_dvd.lean

